- Security: Do not store API keys in the app. Use a backend proxy server to hide the key. The SwiftUI app should call your own backend, which then forwards to the Vicuna endpoint.
- On-device option: Mention that projects like MLC LLM (https://mlc.ai/mlc-llm/) support Vicuna and have iOS examples, but integration with SwiftUI requires bridging Objective-C/C++ code and is non-trivial. Also, model size: Vicuna-7B quantized might be ~4GB, which is large for an app download.
